Subject: [PATCH] Audio stream: the fill for a producer, a clock-driven output for silent runs

ps2_audio_stream::bufferedFrames() / targetFrames(): the frames held for the device now and the
fill it aims at, so a producer whose own clock falls behind real time can keep the output from
running dry (the native sound server mixes ahead by real time then). PS2X_AUDIO_SIM=1 with
PS2X_AUDIO=0: the frames are taken by a clock at 48 kHz instead of a sound card (a thread calling
the device callback), so a silent test run measures the buffer as one with sound would. The
PS2X_AUDIO_STATS line also gives the lowest fill since the last one.
---
diff --git a/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ps2_audio_stream.h b/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ps2_audio_stream.h
index f319085..6e949ae 100644
--- a/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ps2_audio_stream.h
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ps2_audio_stream.h
@@ -16,11 +16,21 @@
 //   PS2X_AUDIO_VOLUME=<f>    0..1 (default 1)
 //   PS2X_AUDIO_DUMP=<file>   writes everything the SPU2 produces to a WAV file
 //                            (16 bit, stereo, 48 kHz), whatever the host plays of it
+//   PS2X_AUDIO_SIM=1         with PS2X_AUDIO=0: the frames taken by a clock at 48 kHz instead
+//                            of a sound card, so a silent run measures the buffer as one with
+//                            sound would (PS2X_AUDIO_STATS: its fill, how often it ran dry)
 namespace ps2_audio_stream
 {
     // Frames of a left and a right sample at 48 kHz, from the thread that runs the IOP.
     void push(const int16_t *samples, size_t frames);
 
+    // The frames held now, which the device plays before anything pushed next; -1 while nothing
+    // takes them (no sound, muted, the device not started yet). For a producer that keeps the
+    // buffer from running dry while its own clock falls behind real time.
+    long long bufferedFrames();
+    // The frames the buffer aims to hold (about 80 ms).
+    size_t targetFrames();
+
     // PS2X_AUDIO and PS2X_AUDIO_VOLUME changed while the game runs (the settings panel, on the
     // window thread): at once.
     void setEnabled(bool on);
